  "worked_solution": "We are told that there are $45$ stairs in the warehouse. The tape diagram for the stairs shows $5$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $45÷5=9.$\n\nNow, we fill the number $9$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/db352d53c2926e7a42b8183088a35860f057f4e5a845554ada955303e3dc8926.png)\n\nSince there are $9$ boxes corresponding to the stairs and carts in total, and each box represents $9$ of these items, the total number of stairs and carts are:\n\n$$\n9\\times 9=81\n$$\n\nSo, there are $81$ stairs and carts altogether.",
